spec ww12-write-after-peer-rollback-explicit: 2 sessions, 6 permutations
# WW12, explicit second writer. s1 writes n and ROLLS BACK; the vacuum is drained
# right after (H1); s2, open since before s1's write, writes n and commits. A write
# after the rollback and drain succeeds in every interleaving; one while s1 is open
# is refused.
# The second writer is an EXPLICIT transaction that BEGINs before
# either session's first step, so its snapshot predates the ROLLBACK. A ROLLBACK
# aborts its transaction (rmp #2973): once it is drained, the older snapshot's write
# must succeed, exactly as the autocommit arm's does. Before #2973 the ROLLBACK
# published a commit record and this write was refused.

starting permutation: s1w s1rb s1dr s2w s2c
step s1w: MATCH (n:Item {name:'n'}) SET n.x = 1 RETURN n.x AS x
x
-
1
(1 row)
step s1rb: ROLLBACK
step s1dr: <vacuum drain>
step s2w: MATCH (n:Item {name:'n'}) SET n.x = 2 RETURN n.x AS x
x
-
2
(1 row)
step s2c: COMMIT
final final: MATCH (n:Item {name:'n'}) RETURN n.x AS x
x
-
2
(1 row)

starting permutation: s1w s2w s1rb s1dr s2c
step s1w: MATCH (n:Item {name:'n'}) SET n.x = 1 RETURN n.x AS x
x
-
1
(1 row)
step s2w: MATCH (n:Item {name:'n'}) SET n.x = 2 RETURN n.x AS x
ERROR: serialization conflict
step s1rb: ROLLBACK
step s1dr: <vacuum drain>
step s2c: COMMIT
ERROR: cypher: transaction poisoned by a prior failed Exec statement — call Rollback
final final: MATCH (n:Item {name:'n'}) RETURN n.x AS x
x
-
0
(1 row)

